# Local control-plane defaults for this machine only.
# Copy to pointer.local.env (gitignored) and edit.
# Loaded by: npm run tauri:dev / tauri:build / Vite (web:dev).
# Already-set OS / CI environment variables always win over this file.
#
# Two modes (same code path):
#   1) No control-plane domains → pure local agent (local models/keys only).
#   2) Domains set → bind that control plane (Pointer's own or an enterprise's — same logic).
#
# If this file is missing, dev/build stay unbound (standalone: local-only).

# --- Mode 1: local-only (default; nothing to set) ---

# --- Mode 2: bind a control plane ---
# A managed build must inject its domains: the source tree hardcodes none, and
# `pointer-core/build.rs` fails the build when POINTER_EDITION=managed is set
# without them. (Enterprise builds use the same keys with their own hosts.)
# Pointer's own release:
# POINTER_EDITION=managed
# VITE_POINTER_EDITION=managed
# POINTER_API_BASE=https://pointer-api.readflowai.com
# POINTER_WEB_BASE=https://pointer.readflowai.com
# VITE_POINTER_WEB_BASE=https://pointer.readflowai.com
# COMPUTER_ANNOTATE_API_BASE=https://pointer-som.readflowai.com
# POINTER_DOWNLOAD_URL=https://pointer.readflowai.com/download

# Enterprise / private control plane (same keys, your hosts):
# POINTER_EDITION=managed
# VITE_POINTER_EDITION=managed
# POINTER_API_BASE=https://pointer-api.example.com
# POINTER_WEB_BASE=https://pointer.example.com
# VITE_POINTER_WEB_BASE=https://pointer.example.com
# COMPUTER_ANNOTATE_API_BASE=https://pointer-som.example.com
# POINTER_DOWNLOAD_URL=https://pointer.example.com/download
